  "ai_language_tip": "Speak clear, polite standard Albanian (sq, Gheg-accented in Kosovo and northern Albania, Tosk in the south); Serbian (sr) is used in Serb-majority municipalities of Kosovo; Italian is understood by many in Albania; English is good among younger staff and in Tirana, Pristina and resorts.",
  "english_ok": "sometimes — Common among younger staff in Tirana, Pristina and tourist areas; limited at public clinics and offices and in villages.",
  "politeness": "Formal 'ju', 'zotëri/zonjë'; open with 'Mirëdita' and say for whom you call; close with 'Faleminderit, mirupafshim'. Warm, relationship-based tone.",
  "name_tip": "Give first name and surname; Albanian surnames do not change by gender but nouns take definite endings (Hoxha / Hoxhaj spellings vary), so spell the name letter by letter.",
  "phone_tip": "al mobile 06x xxx xxxx (10 digits with 0), +355; xk mobile 04x xxx xxx (9 digits with 0), +383; WhatsApp/Viber on the same number common.",
  "time_tip": "'shtatë e gjysmë' = 7:30, 'tetë pa një çerek' = 7:45 (no half-before trap); Serbian 'pola osam' = 7:30 is a trap; read back in 24h.",
  "number_tip": "Albanian uses vigesimal-free decimal counting; 'njëzet' = 20, 'tridhjetë' = 30; prices in lek (al) or euro (xk) — older Albanians may quote 'old lek' (×10), so confirm the amount.",
  "avoid_calling": "Avoid lunch 13:00–15:00, dinner peak 20:00–22:30, calls after 21:00 and Sundays for offices; coffee culture means mornings are busy at cafés.",
  "closed_days": "Shops open on Sundays; holidays: al — 1–2 January, 14 March, 22 March (Nevruz), Easter (Catholic and Orthodox), Eid al-Fitr and Eid al-Adha, 1 May, 28–29 November, 8 and 25 December; xk — 1 January, 17 February, 9 April, 1 and 9 May, Eid holidays, Christmas.",
  "booking_channels": "Phone, WhatsApp, Viber and Instagram dominate for restaurants, salons and guesthouses; Wolt and Baboon for delivery (Tirana, Pristina and other cities); e-Albania for public services; walk-in common for small shops.",
